. This:\n- Develops a piece with tempo\n- Aims directly at f7, the weak square next to Black's king\n- Prevents Black from castling kingside safely\n- Prepares potential attacking ideas\n- Is a principled developing move that creates immediate threats\n\nThe f7 square is only defended by Black's king, and putting pressure there while the king is still in the center is strategically sound.\n\n**Reason:** Developing the bishop to c4 creates immediate pressure on f7, the weakest point in Black's position. With Black's king still on e8 and unable to castle safely, this move maximizes White's attacking chances while developing naturally.\n\n**Answer:** B: f1-c4"}
