osing N: f3-e5+ because it gives check to the exposed Black king on f7, forcing Black to respond to the threat rather than consolidating their material advantage. This knight move centralizes my piece, creates immediate tactical pressure, and the knight from e5 attacks multiple important squares (d7, f7, g6, c6). When behind in material, creating forcing moves and complications is essential rather than allowing the opponent to simply consolidate and convert their advantage.\n\nAnswer: N: f3-e5"}
